      "writtenOn": "2017-01-31T15:55:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This means that users that get a token issued in the same second (before or after) a revocation event is issued will have a revoked token out the door. \n\nBad UX, and not sure the way to fix it short of doing something akin to revocation event issuance is now-1s (which leaves a 1s gap, but would be a better UX). Need to discuss the security implications with the team. \n\nshort story is we err more secure now... but it\u0027s a very bad ux in narrow windows (and some of our tests suck more to write)",
      "parentUuid": "3a461143_b0431b12",
      "revId": "c4881c1c00de436d758c33caf63b1fffb838fed4",
